  "implemented": [
    "Per-session opt-in fixed-capacity native recorder; event reservation and scope/counter recording allocate no memory and never throw.",
    "Scoped native CPU phases, failure/rollback observations, capture-local parents and runtime session/tick labels survive owner replacement.",
    "Guarded start/stop/status/paged-events/summary/export operations share one authority with the human editor; controls do not record themselves.",
    "Overflow seals a retained prefix while open events complete; immutable paging, capture-ID lifetime guards and explicit loss/saturation metadata.",
    "Editor CPU timeline, source filter, selection and cost summaries; partial resource counters use their actual units and latest values.",
    "Renderer lazily enables GPU query collection for active captures; durations remain uncalibrated observations, never invented CPU-aligned spans.",
    "Chrome trace-event export with complete CPU spans and separate GPU/counter observations."
  ],
